## 4. Usage

```go
// Fresh DKG, n=6, t=3
oldRoster := reshare.Roster{IDs: []reshare.ID{1,2,3,4,5,6}, Threshold: 3, Epoch: 1}
old, _ := reshare.RunDKG(oldRoster)

// Proactive reshare to {4,5,6,7,8,9} with t_new=4.
// Old/new overlap is exactly 3 = t_old; only the overlap old members are active.
newRoster := reshare.Roster{IDs: []reshare.ID{4,5,6,7,8,9}, Threshold: 4, Epoch: 2}
res, err := reshare.RunReshare(old, newRoster, reshare.ReshareOptions{
    ActiveOld:      []reshare.ID{4,5,6},
    FileComplaints: true, // honest receivers complain automatically
})
// res.PublicKey == old.PublicKey
// res.Proof.Verify() == nil  -> secret sharing stayed intact
// res.Shares[j]              -> private new share of member j
// res.PublicShares[j]        -> public commitment Y_j

// Any third party proves a member holds its share using pairings:
att := reshare.BuildAttestation(j, res.Shares[j], newRoster.Epoch, res.PublicKey)
ok := reshare.VerifyAttestation(att, res.PublicShares[j], newRoster.Epoch, res.PublicKey)
```

